#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128784 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d3a0d58-20a3-570d-91e7-aa8f10dafb5a" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Triple Integral as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "5f6a3dd8-65fb-5e1f-aa19-d0115c9aa217" :question/math-academy-id "e-11585" :question/problem "Express the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_{R} (x+y+z)^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V$\nover the box\n$R = \\bigg\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0\\leq z \\leq 2 \\bigg\\}$\nas a repeated integral of the form\n$\\displaystyle \\int_a^b \\int_c^d \\int_e^f \\ldots \\: \\textrm{d}y\\: \\textrm{d}z\\: \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Given the limits for $x,y$, and $z$, we can express our triple integral as a repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∭_(R)(x + y + z)^{2}dV &= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{-1}^{2}(x + y + z)^{2}dydzdx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128789 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "ff5e1f9e-d67d-5264-b556-2f7b3a946c3f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12391" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, evaluate the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the rectangular box $R = \\left\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\:0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: -1 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 1 \\leq z \\leq 3 \\right\\}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} z-xy \\: \\textrm{d}V = \\int_{-1}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{1}^{3} z-xy \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nSince we're integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, we write\n\n$$\n\\textrm d V = \\textrm d z\\:\\textrm d x\\:\\textrm d y\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}∫_{1}^{3}z - xydzdxdy &= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[∫_{1}^{3}z - xydz]dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}[\\frac{1}{2}z^{2} - xyz]_{z = 1}^{z = 3}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(9 - 1) - xy(3 - 1)dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2xydxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2xydxdy &= ∫_{-1}^{1}[∫_{0}^{2}4 - 2yxdx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}[4x - yx^{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = 2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}4(2 - 0) - y(2^{2} - 0)dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-1}^{1}8 - 4ydy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{1}8 - 4ydy &= [8y - 2y^{2}]_{y =-1}^{y = 1} \\\\\n&= 8(1 - (-1)) - 2(1^{2} - (-1)^{2}) \\\\\n&= 8 \\cdot 2 - 2(1 - 1) \\\\\n&= 16 - 0 \\\\\n&= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128949 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "9a9885cc-6a93-57ee-bfd0-b4285395e326" :question/math-academy-id "e-7263" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_{R} y \\cos{x} \\sin{z} \\: \\textrm{d}V$\nover the box $R = \\bigg\\{(x,y,z) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\pi \\bigg\\}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express our triple integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∭_(R)y\\cos x\\sin zdV &= ∫_{0}^{π}∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{π/2}y\\cos x\\sin zdxdydz\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of integration\n\n$$\nR = \\left[0,\\pi/2\\right]\\times[0,1]\\times\\left[0,\\pi\\right]\n$$\n\nis a rectangular box, and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z)$, we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n∫_{0}^{π/2}\\cos xdx∫_{0}^{1}ydy∫_{0}^{π}\\sin zdz\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{π/2}\\cos xdx∫_{0}^{1}ydy∫_{0}^{π}\\sin zdz &= [\\sin x]_{0}^{π/2} \\cdot [\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{1} \\cdot [- \\cos z]_{0}^{π} \\\\\n&= (1 - 0) \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2} - 0) \\cdot (1 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1332369-dd6a-5c32-a313-2d84eb73cdd9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5423789-1e08-5a57-9551-8ac6459cc9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126507} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf388d2-e394-5178-8740-8d5930578fa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126508} {:answer/id #uuid "dc46bf67-ff25-57c6-81da-fc7cc95cf285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(e^{2} - 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126509} {:answer/id #uuid "f95f9667-8a24-5ea6-b059-467599e685f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126510} {:answer/id #uuid "7012b9cb-9f58-5777-b6c9-98f70c788057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5423789-1e08-5a57-9551-8ac6459cc9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126507} :answer-field/id #uuid "7652d5fb-da25-50aa-81fe-e299053395cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126506}] :question/id #uuid "9ce80f42-293e-5e66-a70f-dd95799ecbec" :question/math-academy-id "q-161374" :question/problem "By integrating first with respect to $z$, then $x$, and then $y$, evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)(x - y)e^{z}dV$\nover the rectangular box $R = {(x, y, z): 0 \\le x \\le 1,-1 \\le y \\le 0, \\ln 2 \\le z \\le 2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3683ffbc-6a20-57c6-93e1-0eb7236e3752" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8da11700-fec0-5bc3-a000-ef6d8869ed80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127845} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2c85a1-440d-5a3e-8973-080c6fe40c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127846} {:answer/id #uuid "336b0d75-478d-51be-b6e4-c7a7a06faaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127847} {:answer/id #uuid "40170cf1-f81e-552e-adeb-a0ea3f961415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127848} {:answer/id #uuid "67ea7c30-f76f-520e-a761-1516d9a33ecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8da11700-fec0-5bc3-a000-ef6d8869ed80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127845} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fcfe628-79f8-5403-9aa4-4d36aab5a2a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127844}] :question/id #uuid "8712bce7-9b2f-578f-98a6-ec22ffc6519a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39475" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$∭_(R)\\frac{e^{z + y}}{x}dV$,\nover the box $R = {(x, y, z): 1 \\le x \\le e, 0 \\le y \\le \\ln 3, 0 \\le z \\le \\ln 2}$."}]}
